Z||000000||sqoach||03-29-2001||05:52 PM||||as my car was running today, i noticed a hole in my muffler. it's rusting out at the seam. since i planned on getting a new system anyway, i guess this happened at about the right time.<BR>but i don't know what to get. i don't really care about performance gains. just need something that doesn't sound like a lawnmower.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>i'm also considering replacing the cat. it's the factory one and it's probably gonna bite the dust in a few months.<P>any suggestions greatly appreciated. i don't have much money at all, so i'm gonna have to sell some stuff. so, the cheaper the better (to an extent)<BR>also, i want to find one that will last a long time. no point of getting something cheap if it's not gonna last.<BR>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||stsmithgt||03-29-2001||07:27 PM||||Been there done that.  I didn't have much money to sink into it either.<BR>  It's a good idea to call around to several shops large and small, even ones out of your area.  Of course some of the small ones didn't know what a Fiero was. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  It might be worth the drive.  One of the places I checked was a Midas here in Monterey CA., and they wanted at least $300.00 to change the muffler only.  I called a Midas up near my parents(3 hours north)since I was going to visit them anyway and they wanted $100.00 for the same parts and labor.  Guess where I went?  I suppose performance parts would have been cool, but the money thing was there.  At least I have a warrenty. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>I hit a half price sale for the CAT at the same place.  My car is stock anyway. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||03-29-2001||07:27 PM||||go to autozone buy the cat there, they have a lifetime warranty on them. as for mufflers, well i guess any muffler will do,but if it was me i would get a flowie or something similar that will last,plus it costs just about the same as if you were to buy a regular muffler.good luck<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <BR>86gt ported and polished heads,ported manifolds,k&n air filter,holley side scoop, deck lid scoop,rear swaybar,flowmaster 80 series.<BR>84 indy 4 speed <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||03-30-2001||06:48 PM||||well i did a little shopping around. just to the only two places in town that i know of. both places have to special order it, and it's gonna be near $200 for a cat-back system. now i've seen the fierostore's stock replacement. and it's a lot cheaper. is it any good?<BR>i could also get this muffler shop in town to do a custom job. but that might cost a lot too. the owner is a friend of my dad's. but who knows. the main problem he was showing me was the sharp bend right before the muffler. he said it's hard to make bends like that. i also found a replacement cat for $70 at o'reillys. is that a pretty good deal?||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||03-30-2001||08:56 PM||||$70 for a cat sound good.  Is it weld-on or clamp-on?  I got Rodney Dickman's cat with stainless steel extension pipes and clamps for about $120.  My muffler also is showing signs of rust-through but I haven't yet researched a replacement.<BR>||||reg||1
